  "data_description_en": "1. Taiwan's assisted-reproduction database was established in ROC year 87 (1998); assisted-reproduction institutions periodically report cases treated at their facility (excluding artificial insemination between spouses). 2. The Assisted Reproduction Data Reporting and Management Regulations were made under Article 27(2) of the Assisted Reproduction Act. 3. The 'Assisted Reproduction Data Reporting Regulations' were promulgated in full (15 articles) by DOH order Shou-Guo-Zi No. 0960400731 on 8 August 2007 and took effect on the promulgation date. 4. Data that institutions must report: (i) donor health exams and assessments; (ii) results of procedures using donated gametes; (iii) data on donated gametes or resulting embryos not completed for donation, returned, destroyed, re-donated, or transferred; (iv) cases starting ovulation drugs; (v) assisted-reproduction case data; (vi) destruction of the couple's gametes or embryos. 5. Drug-start years span ROC 87 to 112 (1998-2023).",
  "notes_en": "1. The patient basic information file (H_BHP_PST_MASTER) and smear test data file (H_BHP_PST_SMEAR) may have blank and duplicate IDs, which should be noted during comparison. 2. The infection (INFECTION) field in the smear test file is a multiple choice question; care must be taken when extracting for analysis.",
